# `&` is integer-only. The float types declare `+ - * / %` and the six
# comparisons but no bitwise AND, so `f32 & f32` is a missing-method error
# rather than C the compiler cannot build: gcc rejects `&` on two floats,
# and an operator that typechecks must emit code that compiles.
main: function is {
    a: 1.5.f32
    b: 2.5.f32
    c: a & b
    print "\{c}"
}
